{"id":"a85a7c7a-b9e5-4f9a-afdb-95e34a022af2","object":"chat.completion","created":1785029048,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"import math\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    matrix = case['matrix']\\n    if not matrix or not isinstance(matrix, list):\\n        raise ValueError('Matrix must be a non-empty list')\\n    n_rows = len(matrix)\\n    n_cols = len(matrix[0])\\n    for row in matrix:\\n        if len(row) != n_cols:\\n            raise ValueError('Matrix rows must have equal length')\\n    # document frequency per column\\n    df = [0] * n_cols\\n    for row in matrix:\\n        for j, val in enumerate(row):\\n            if val != 0:\\n                df[j] += 1\\n    # IDF as log(1 + total_rows / (1 + df))\\n    idf = [math.log(1.0 + n_rows / (1.0 + d)) for d in df]\\n    # weighted matrix\\n    weighted_matrix = []\\n    for row in matrix:\\n        weighted_row = [round(val * idf[j], 6) for j, val in enumerate(row)]\\n        weighted_matrix.append(weighted_row)\\n    # row degree (sum of weighted entries per row)\\n    row_degree = [round(sum(row), 6) for row in weighted_matrix]\\n    return {\\n        'idf': [round(v, 6) for v in idf],\\n        'weighted_matrix': weighted_matrix,\\n        'row_degree': row_degree\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python source for solve(case) that, given a payload with \"matrix\" (list of lists of numbers), computes IDF, weighted_matrix, and row_degree as per description. Also note: the output schema requires idf (array of numbers), row_degree (array of numbers), weighted_matrix (2D array of numbers). The description says: \"For each feature count rows with a nonzero entry. Compute IDF as log(1 + number_of_rows / (1 + document_frequency)). Multiply every entry by its feature IDF and sum weighted rows for degree. Round and return IDF, weighted matrix, and row degrees.\" Also note: They mention \"self-similarity_removed\"